Where the entry is written depends on how far initialisation got.
Once [[repo]] exists we know which project the failure belongs to; a
failure before that---an unreadable working directory, a Git that will
not start---has no project yet, and [[report_error]] falls back to the
current directory, writing only if a [[.learnlog/]] is already there.

<<functions>>=
def _report_swallowed_failure(context, error):
    """Send an exception we must not raise to the diagnostics path."""
    report_error(
        context, error,
        repo.workdir if repo is not None else None,
    )
