Reaching the next line means both statements are silent, and there the
two callers part company.

An interpreter that [[learnlog init]] wired for autostart has already
been told which project it serves; the marker file next to its [[.pth]]
hook is that instruction (\cref{sec:autostart}).
If neither the marker nor the [[sys.prefix]] backup resolves, the
instruction has been \emph{lost}---the project was deleted, or the
marker was left behind by a project that no longer exists---and the one
thing we know is that the answer is not \enquote{wherever the student
happens to be standing}.
Guessing there is how a stale marker in a development venv turned every
run into a fresh repository in an unrelated directory.
So a wired interpreter with no resolvable project logs nothing at all.

<<refuse to guess for a wired interpreter>>=
