The remaining caller is the explicit
\mintinline{python}{import learnlog} that a student adds by hand on a
machine where no venv could be wired (\cref{learnlog}).
Nothing has stated a project, so \enquote{where am I} is the only
question left, and creating a fresh repository in the current directory
is what makes that first run work with no setup at all.

The current directory is subject to the same bound as the search above
it.
A home directory is not a project, so a bare
\mintinline{python}{import learnlog} run from [[$HOME]] itself must not
start a repository whose worktree is everything the student owns.
There is no better guess to fall back on, and inventing a directory
would be worse than doing nothing, so this too refuses.
The student sees no difference---that is the transparency requirement---
and [[LEARNLOG_DEBUG]] explains it to anyone who asks
(\cref{sec:diagnostics}).

