Unit tests can only show that the pieces agree with each other.
The claim that matters is about a whole process---the wrapper has to
be installed before the student's code runs, survive it, and reach the
commit---so the regression tests run real scripts and read the trailer
back out of the log repository.
This helper removes the boilerplate they would otherwise repeat.
It launches [[python -S]] with the checkout's [[src/]] on
[[PYTHONPATH]], mirroring [[run_explicit_import]] above: skipping
[[site.py]] keeps the installed [[.pth]] hook out of the way, so the
run under test is the one the script itself starts.
The [[exit()]] built-in is the exception---it only exists when
[[site.py]] has run---so that one test asks for [[site]].
We cannot disable a possibly installed [[.pth]] hook there with
[[LEARNLOG_SKIP_AUTOSTART]], because that variable is a real opt-out
(\cref{sec:initialize}) and would silence the explicit import too.
What we can do is take the question of \emph{where} out of the hook's
hands by exporting [[LEARNLOG_PROJECT_ROOT]] for that run.
Every source defers to it (\cref{sec:initialize}), so the run lands in
the temporary directory whether the hook fires or not, and the test
stops depending on how the developer's own venv happens to be wired---
a venv whose marker points at a project that no longer exists would
otherwise make the run decline to log at all.
The deployed configuration the deferred [[site.setquit]] hook exists
for is reproduced either way:

<<test helpers>>=
def run_and_read_commit(source, *, workdir, env, name, with_site=False):
    """Run ``source`` as a script and return result and commit message."""
    script = pathlib.Path(workdir) / name
    script.write_text(source)
    run_env = env.copy()
    source_root = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / "src"
    pythonpath = str(source_root)
    existing_pythonpath = run_env.get("PYTHONPATH")
    if existing_pythonpath:
        pythonpath = pythonpath + os.pathsep + existing_pythonpath
    run_env["PYTHONPATH"] = pythonpath
    command = [sys.executable]
    if not with_site:
        command.append("-S")
    else:
        run_env["LEARNLOG_PROJECT_ROOT"] = str(workdir)
    command.append(str(script))
    result = subprocess.run(
        command,
        cwd=str(workdir), env=run_env,
        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30,
    )
    message = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "--git-dir=.learnlog", "--work-tree=.",
         "log", "-1", "--format=%B"],
        cwd=str(workdir),
        capture_output=True, text=True,
    ).stdout
    return result, message
@

