A ``.pth`` file in the venv's ``site-packages`` imports this
module and calls ``autostart()``, which imports ``learnlog`` and
lets its ``initialize()`` decide whether to log this interpreter
invocation.  This module only resolves *which* project a run
belongs to, from the venv rather than from the working directory.

Imports nothing from ``learnlog``: importing ``learnlog._autostart``
already runs ``learnlog/__init__.py``, so any back-import would fire
during a partially initialised package import.

Test-friendly: each helper accepts optional overrides so unit tests
can exercise the resolver without monkeypatching ``sys`` or the
filesystem wholesale.
"""
